WEBVTT

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.250
The date is 1969.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.810
The setting is Japan in a period
of advanced economic growth.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.970
This is the story of those who protect
mankind from the grasp of invaders.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.580
This is the story
of The Gate Keepers.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:36.100
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.280
<i>Chikara to chikara butsukareba,
When power collides with power,</i>

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.880
<i>arasoi wa hajimaru.
wars start.</i>

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.420
<i>Tatakau koto ga</i> yuuki <i>to</i>
I <i>don't think fighting</i>

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.420
<i>omowanai kedo...
equals bravery, but...</i>

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.830
<i>...mamoritai yo
...I want to protect</i>

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.390
kimi <i>no sono egao.
that smile on your face.</i>

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.000
<i>Asu e no geeto
We can't see the gate</i>

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.700
<i>mienai keredo...
to tomorrow, but...</i>

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.470
<i>dare ni</i> demo <i>aru yo.
one's inside each of us.</i>

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.140
<i>Let's open the gate!</i>

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.850
Kinou <i>no namida</i> wa
<i>The tears we shed yesterday</i>

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.110
<i>kitto muda ja nai.
are probably not in vain.</i>

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.490
<i>Arasoi no nai</i> mirai wa
<i>A future without war</i>

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:29.250
<i>ano tobira no mukougawa.
waits behind that door.</i>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.390
Mune <i>no oku</i> fukaku
<i>Retrieve the key lying</i>

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.330
<i>Jitto shimaikonda
deep inside your heart,</i>

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:39.130
<i>kagi wo takaku kakagete,
hold it up high,</i>

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.370
<i>fumidasou!
and step out!</i>

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.670
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:52.200
<i>You can open the gate!</i>

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.980
<i>You are aware of
the frequent airplane accidents...</i>

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:17.020
<i>occuring worldwide over the
past several days, aren't you?</i>

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.200
<i>Yes, sir! That's why
Rurippe and Kaoru...</i>

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.110
<i>...have been specially assigned
to Haneda Airport, right?</i>

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.150
<i>Yes...</i>

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.720
Today, we spotted a flying object...

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:32.050
"suspected to be an invader
over the Sea of Japan.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.050
A gate keeper from the
Shanghai branch gave pursuit...

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.350
...but lost sight of
the object over Japan.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.520
There are gate keepers
in Shanghai, too?

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.530
This is the file.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.500
The pursuit plane
carrying the gate keeper...

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.060
...lost combat functions
and landed at the Atsugi base.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.540
Captain Ukiya, I want you to
link up with the gate keeper...

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.970
...and assist in the
search for the invader.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.340
Roger, AEGIS!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.830
<i>"Captain " Ukiya...</i>

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.880
Let's see who is the gate keeper
from the Shanghai branch...

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.810
...what's this?

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.560
Oh, nuts!

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.490
MEDICAL ROOM

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.000
Why am I such a klutz...?

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.560
Huh?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.110
To Ukiya: Shanghai G.K.. Top Secret Data
I accidentally gave Ukiya an empty file!

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.700
I have to report this to
the commander immediately...

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.610
...but the last time, I
accidentally handed him...

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:38.660
...my poetry diary
instead of a report.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.480
I got a thorn
in my index finger!

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.030
I need a bandage!

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.720
Bancho!

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.670
Thank God! You're the
only one I can turn to!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.840
Who, me?

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.370
I'm touched,
Princess Secretary!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.570
My name is Keiko Ochiai.
I want you to deliver...

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.750
...this file to Ukiya in Atsugi.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.260
To Ukiya?

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.790
Yes!

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.150
Understood, Princess Secretaryfl

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.030
just a moment!

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:23.860
Didn't you have something to
see me about? Me, Keiko Ochiai?

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.530
Oh, yeah...

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.100
...but it doesn't matter now.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.640
You're bleeding!

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.100
MEDICAL ROOM

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:40.770
l, Chotaro Banba, could die
for you, Princess Secretary.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.640
l am on my way!

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.590
My name is Keiko Ochiai!!

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.580
ATSUGI AIR BASE

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.400
Self Defense Forces

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:18.210
<i>The gate keeper is expecting me too.
lf I go,</i> I'll <i>find them.</i>

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:25.220
<i>I sure am glad that Rurippe isn 't
here. lf she were, she'd say ..</i>

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.700
<i>”...didn 't you check the file?
You have no attention span!"</i>

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:32.060
<i>"You're a failure as Captain. "
That 's what she'd say for sure.</i>

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.630
PASS
Please put this on your left breast.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:37.130
<i>I wonder what the
special assignment is.</i>

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:39.470
<i>What are Rurippe and Kaoru
doing at Haneda Airport?</i>

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:46.380
Airplane accidents are
frequently occurring worldwide.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:50.020
According to a report from AEGIS
intelligence, paranormal frequencies...

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.920
...are also being registered in
the vicinity of Haneda Airport.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:58.150
I want you to guard the airport.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:04.170
These are special uniforms prepared
by the AEGIS costuming department...

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:05.890
...especially for this mission.

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.240
<i>Uniforms to wear at an airport?</i>

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:13.900
Tidy uniforms for assisting others?
Uniforms that all girls want to wear?

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:18.470
Well, they certainly assist
to tidy things for others...

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:20.170
Yes, sir! I'll do it!

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.850
Me, too, sir!

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:26.910
Are you sure? I would think
Captain Ukiya would be more suitable.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.260
Don't be ridiculous,
sir! I'll do it!

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.360
When it comes to love of
peace and our green land...

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:40.400
...and the fervent desire to
defend mankind from invaders...

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:41.900
...l am second to none!

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.500
Me, too, sir!

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.270
V- Very well.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.840
Since you insist, I will let you do it.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.850
Yes, sir!

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:56.880
"Airport” normally equals "stewardess."
What the heck is this?!

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.880
Excuse me, are you free?

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.520
The commander could have
mentioned something!

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.530
E- Excuse me?

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.560
- Ikusawa!
- Huh? What?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.900
Oh, I'm sorry. Have a seat.

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.790
Maybe I should get
mine done, too...

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.390
Yes sir!
Please have a seat!

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.340
<i>Ikusawa, l challenge you to see
who can shine the most shoes!</i>

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:22.940
<i>And if I win,</i>
I <i>get Ukiya's heart!</i>

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.080
<i>Kaoru...</i>

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.140
<i>I don 't know whats going 0n,
but you're on fire.</i>

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.650
<i>I can't let you beat me!</i>

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:42.560
Hey. what's going on?

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.830
Those two look like
cute shoe-shine girls.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.300
Which should I get to do mine?

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:16.660
Ukki-yah! Ukki-yah! Where are you?!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:18.960
Ukki-yah!

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.260
Ukki-yah! Come out!

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:22.900
If you mean me, I'm over here.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:27.570
What? I'm busy now.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.670
I must find Ukki-yah
or l'm in trouble.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.880
I told you, I <i>am</i> Ukiya!

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:39.380
Ukki-yah is not funny like you!

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:43.450
I told you, I'm Shun Ukiya!
You're the one who's funny!

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:48.400
I'm not funny.
My name is Fen Feiling. Oops.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.930
I do not have time for this.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:52.630
Hey!

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.400
Hey, you. What's a high school student
like you doing in a place like this?

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.340
- Excuse me, sir!!
- Hey, wait!!

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.770
Hey! I keep telling you,
I'M Ukiya!

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:07.150
<i>This is search chopper 302,
presently above the Sumidz River.</i>

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.180
<i>Unable to spot invaders!</i>

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:14.650
<i>Search chopper 303,
all normal above Tokyo Tower!</i>

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:16.190
<i>Nothing suspicious spotted!</i>

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.750
<i>This is patrol ship Akzuki.</i>

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:22.660
<i>No invaders detected in
Tokyo Bay District-A!</i>

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:27.030
Where have they vanished?

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.070
We must find the invaders
interfering with sky transit...

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:36.440
...a necessity for the future. We must
find and exterminate them at any cost!

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.680
<i>This is control tower,
this is control tower.</i>

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:44.280
<i>Air France Flight 274, please
approach 290m south-southeast.</i>

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:50.690
<i>This is Air France Flight 274.
Roger. We are setting down now.</i>

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.400
Regarding the jumbo jet that made
an emergency landing this morning...

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.070
...how long is it staying here?

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:14.410
I authorized it. The bigger
the plane, the better?!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.040
Do you have a problem with that?!

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.710
N- No, not really.

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:23.120
Come on, you! Get back
to work! No slacking offl

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:28.230
Hey, don't use a lighter in here!!

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:32.730
You have no right
ordering me around, moron.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:37.240
Good grief. Why doesn't she get it?
I keep telling her I'm Ukiya...

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:39.130
- Hey, wait!
-Catch him!

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:43.610
Take that!

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:46.840
An Earth Defense license?!

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.750
Don't tell me you're...

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.580
You're...

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:56.250
...the gate keeper from
the Shanghai branch?!

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:08.100
That'll be 28,760 yen.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:11.460
That much?!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.100
Give me a receipt, please.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.110
Ukiya, where are you?!

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.850
Ukki-yah, where are you?
Ukki-yah!!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.590
Oops. Wait a minute!

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.150
Are you looking for Ukiya, too?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.630
Ukki-yah is missing,
so I'm having trouble.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:35.130
Does that mean you're
the Shanghai gate super?

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:37.630
Aiya! You're a gate keeper!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.130
Ikusawa, how many pairs did you polish?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.570
46. How about you?

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:47.440
46 here, too.
It's a tie, for now...

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:50.640
Excuse me, could I
get mine done, as well?

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:55.870
I'll do them! Let me do them!

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:00.490
I'm sorry. You seem
so tired, too...

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:02.180
No problem whatsoever!

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:06.930
We're going to be seeing
your mother after one year...

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.560
...so we must look our best.

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:12.970
All right, can I go look at
the planes in the meantime?

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.500
Won't you get lost?

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.330
Aw, I will not!

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:18.500
Really...? No, it's a bad idea.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.170
Come on, Grampa!

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.650
All right, I'll go with you.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:30.850
So, your mother has been working
in New York all this time?

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:32.680
- Yeah.
- I see.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:34.650
- Here.
- Thanks.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:37.220
How about your father?

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.560
He's a pilot. He's cool.
He's in Europe right now.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:44.900
Wow. Then you don't get to see
your parents very much, huh?

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.560
Aren't you lonely?

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.970
I have Grampa and Grandma.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.340
I see. Good for you!

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.240
Oh, a plane is landing.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.610
Do you suppose that's
the one your mother's on?

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.370
That's a Douglas DC-8.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:07.750
Mom's on a Boeing 727. The tail
wing is shaped differently.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.020
You know a lot about planes.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:12.790
Yeah. In my class, they
call me "Dr. Airplane."

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:15.660
Wow...
Okay, what's that one?

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:19.860
That's a...
...Boeing 737!

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:21.900
They just came to Japan this month.

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:25.670
The one over there is a DC-7,
and in front is a YS-11.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.680
Propeller planes work hard, too!

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.500
Very impressive, Dr. Airplane.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:34.140
What's wrong?

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:39.680
Mom and Dad are always in
airplanes because of their jobs.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.490
Do you know about the accident
3 days ago in Amsterdam?

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:50.290
Yes. A plane barged onto the runway
when a passenger jet was landing...

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.730
...and the plane trying
to land was... you know.

00:14:55.170 --> 00:15:00.700
My dad's plane was above awaiting
its turn to land when it happened.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:04.910
Northwest Airlines Flight 403
is 15 minutes behind schedule...

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.740
...now landing shortly.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.580
- Kazushige.
- Grampa!

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:15.320
Your mother's plane, Flight 403,
will be landing soon.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.420
The lady bought me juice!

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:20.950
Oh, thank you. How much did it cost?

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.630
Please, don't worry about it.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:27.600
In exchange, he taught me
lots about airplanes, right?

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.730
Wow, airports really are dramatic!

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:33.640
Say, is that one of the jumbos
I keep hearing about?

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:35.040
Huh? Where?

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:37.810
That one there! I'm sure of it!

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:40.280
Aw, I wish my little
brothers could see this...

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:44.180
It can't be a jumbo jet! They don't
go into commission until next year!

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.720
What?!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.720
Then what is that?!

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:55.160
I'm Shun Ukiya from the Far East
branch... Hey, are you listening?

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.760
This way, sir.

00:15:58.070 --> 00:16:00.360
Ukiya, so there you are!

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:01.700
Huh?

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.640
Ukki-yah!

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.000
You!

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:06.630
What is wrong, Ukki-yah?

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:11.680
<i>The Ministry of Transportation is
establishing a course of action...</i>

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:14.240
<i>to pass on the airfare
price hike, but the union...</i>

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:15.680
Where is this?!

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.310
It's Haneda Airport.

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:19.080
Take me there! Hurry!

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:34.100
<i>Invaders spotted! They are disguised
as a jumbo jet at Haneda Airport.</i>

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.680
Hmm?! They intend to gather
invaders from all over the world...

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:52.220
...to evolve their
metamorphosis of flight!

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.920
Don't let the invader
jumbo jet take offl!

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.720
Launch the NF-104A!

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.670
Launch gate open!

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.750
Ooh, intense!

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.400
- Faster, faster!!
- This is as fast as it can go!

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.740
Don't let the invader
jumbo jet take off!

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:50.400
Yes, lkusawa!

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.910
GATE OPEN!

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:07.560
At this rate, it will take off!

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:12.500
Now that I'm here,
everything will be all right!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.880
Reiko!!

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:29.250
At her speed, she'll be
in Kyushu in a few minutes.

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:33.050
<i>This is Flight 403.
We have no more fuel. We are landfing.</i>

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:38.250
Say, isn't that plane
attempting to land?

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:42.250
Don't tell me that's the plane
carrying the boy's mother!

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:54.600
Oh, no! It'll take off.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.070
Ukiyal!

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:03.250
Vacuous Missile!!

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:16.990
Ya-hoo!

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:27.000
The central core is unharmed!!

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:32.150
Damn!

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:56.170
Megane?

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:59.730
<i>Ukiya!I brought the gate engine!</i>

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:07.280
- Wait!
- Hey!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.320
I'll use the gate engine!

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:11.510
Wait a secondl!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.960
Hey... That's a Concord!!

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.600
- Ukiya, why are you just standing there?!
- Uh, I...

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.770
- Who is that girl, Ukiya?!
- She's a gate keeper...

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:51.820
<i>It is my fault.
I didn't shoot it down proper/y...</i>

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:56.090
Ukki-yah, tell me where
the red core is.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:59.030
I will not let him
into the sky again.

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.480
Gate open!
KAl-MEN!!

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:35.530
Explosive Panda Fire Ball!

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:48.550
Hey, she did it!

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:51.910
That's Tokyo for you.
They sure like to show off.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.420
- Here's your receipt.
- Oh, thank you.

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:57.330
- Mom!!
- Kazushige!

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:03.430
She left with all the glory.

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:06.060
The keeper of the Gate of Fire, huh...?

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:09.260
And possibly my second rival!

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:11.770
I'm sorry, Ukki-yah!!

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:21.520
It looks like fun to be
a Japanese gate keeper!

00:22:24.190 --> 00:22:26.310
I am going to join them!!

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:40.540
<i>Itsumademo wasurenai
We received many things</i>

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:44.400
<i>takusan no mono moratta ne.
we will never forget.</i>

00:22:44.510 --> 00:22:49.380
<i>Sora no iro utsushite hikaru
I don't mean the blue jewels flashing</i>

00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:52.750
<i>aoi houseki ya
with colors of the sky...</i>

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:54.880
koinu-tachi
or a big yard

00:22:54.880 --> 00:23:00.050
<i>hanemawaru hiroi</i> niwaja <i>nai,
with puppies romping around,</i>

00:23:00.050 --> 00:23:03.390
motto motto daijina
but something <i>much</i> more

00:23:03.390 --> 00:23:08.020
<i>mono wo.
important.</i>

00:23:08.730 --> 00:23:12.890
<i>Kinou Kara kyou e
From yesterday to today,</i>

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:17.530
<i>kyou kara asu e to
from today to tomorrow,</i>

00:23:18.010 --> 00:23:24.310
boku-tachi wa aruite yuku yo.
we will walk toward the future.
